{"type":"standard","title":"Badyara language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Badyara language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q35095","titles":{"canonical":"Badyara_language","normalized":"Badyara language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Badyara language</span></span>"},"pageid":33151739,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1355482654","tid":"13bafdcc-558c-11f1-ac62-8bff40bfbf2c","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:12:34Z","description":"Niger–Congo language of West Africa","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badyara_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badyara_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badyara_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Badyara_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badyara_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Badyara_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badyara_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Badyara_language"}},"extract":"Badyara is an Eastern Senegal-Guinea language of Guinea and Guinea-Bissau. Variants of the name are Badara, Badian, Badjara, Badyaranké; there are also Jaad, Bigola, Gola, Kanjad [ka-njad(ɛ)]), Pajade, Pajadinka.","extract_html":"<p><b>Badyara</b> is an Eastern Senegal-Guinea language of Guinea and Guinea-Bissau. Variants of the name are <i>Badara, Badian, Badjara, Badyaranké;</i> there are also <i>Jaad, Bigola, Gola, Kanjad </i>[ka-njad(ɛ)]<i>), Pajade, Pajadinka</i>.</p>"}